<div class="calcpad-output">
 <!-- Embed a [glTF 3D model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GlTF) directly in a CalcpadCE worksheet using the Google [`<model-viewer>`](https://modelviewer.dev) web component.
<p>Combine the rotating CAD preview with parametric bolt resistance calculations to produce richly illustrated structural connection reports. </p>
<p></p>
<p>Copy the code into the Desktop application to change the parameters in real-time. -->
 <script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/model-viewer/3.0.1/model-viewer.min.js" type="module">
 </script>
 <model-viewer alt="bolt_and_nut.glb" auto-rotate="" camera-controls="" class="side" field-of-view="8deg" shadow-intensity="0.5" src="./Models/bolt_and_nut.glb" style="height:280pt;">
 </model-viewer>
 <h4>Loads (for one bolt)</h4>
 <p>
  Tension -
  <span class="eq">
   <var>F</var>
   <sub>t_Ed</sub>
   =
   <u class="input-8">20</u>
  </span>
  kN
 </p>
 <p>
  Shear -
  <span class="eq">
   <var>F</var>
   <sub>v_Ed</sub>
   =
   <u class="input-9">10</u>
  </span>
  kN
 </p>
 <h4>Bolt data</h4>
 <p id="bolt" style="display:none;">
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   =
   <u class="input-11">12</u>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  Bolt diameter -
  <select data-target="bolt">
   <option value="12">M12</option>
   <option value="14">M14</option>
   <option value="16">M16</option>
   <option value="18">M18</option>
   <option value="20">M20</option>
   <option value="22">M22</option>
   <option value="24">M24</option>
   <option value="27">M27</option>
   <option value="30">M30</option>
   <option value="36">M36</option>
  </select>
 </p>
 <p>
  Bolt diameter -
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   = 12
  </span>
  mm
 </p>
 <p>
  Hole diameter -
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   <sub>0</sub>
   = 13
  </span>
  mm
 </p>
 <p>
  Punching diameter-
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   <sub>m</sub>
   = 20.5
  </span>
  mm
 </p>
 <p>
  Area of the unthreaded part (gross) -
  <span class="eq">
   <var>A</var>
   =
   <span class="dvc">
    <var>π</var>
    ·
    <var>d</var>
    <sup>2</sup>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    4
   </span>
   =
   <span class="dvc">
    3.14 · 12
    <sup>2</sup>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    4
   </span>
   = 113.1
  </span>
  mm²
 </p>
 <p>
  Area of the threaded part (net) -
  <span class="eq">
   <var>A</var>
   <sub>s</sub>
   = 84
  </span>
  mm²
 </p>
 <p id="grade" style="display:none;">
  <span class="eq">
   <var>Grade</var>
   =
   <u class="input-54">10.9</u>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  Bolt steel grade -
  <select data-target="grade">
   <option value="4.6">4.6</option>
   <option value="4.8">4.8</option>
   <option value="5.6">5.6</option>
   <option value="5.8">5.8</option>
   <option value="6.8">6.8</option>
   <option value="8.8">8.8</option>
   <option value="10.9">10.9</option>
  </select>
 </p>
 Bolt steel grade - 10.9
